# The kitty keyboard protocol's flag 1, disambiguate escape codes, on the
# keys that the specification names and that no other flag 1 scenario
# presses. Ctrl+C, Escape with Ctrl or Alt, Alt+Space and Ctrl+Shift+Alt+A
# are each sent as CSI code ; modifiers u. Ctrl+Shift+Tab is CSI 9 ; 6 u,
# because Shift+Tab is not a key of its own. A non-ASCII key with Alt or
# Ctrl is CSI u with its code point, and alone it sends its text. A key
# that makes no text carries Caps Lock and NumLock in its modifiers. F2
# with no modifier is CSI Q, and F4 with Alt is CSI 1 ; 3 S. A keypad key
# that makes text sends it with Shift, and is CSI u with its own number
# with Ctrl.
# spec: kitty's Comprehensive keyboard handling in terminals: Disambiguate escape codes, Modifiers, Legacy key event encoding, Functional key definitions, Bugs in fixterms
# covers: input.kitty-keyboard
size 20 2
send "\e[>1u"
key c mods=ctrl
key Escape mods=ctrl
key Escape mods=alt
key space mods=alt
key A mods=shift+ctrl+alt
key ISO_Left_Tab mods=shift+ctrl
key eacute
key eacute mods=alt
key eacute mods=ctrl
key Up mods=lock
key F5 mods=num
key Delete mods=ctrl+num
key F2
key F4 mods=alt
key End mods=ctrl
key KP_Equal mods=shift+num char="="
key KP_Multiply mods=ctrl+num char="*"
